From dbe969572b68cba9a116180f14b97cd17c61b457 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild Idler Bot <bot@guildidler.local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 01:01:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] New-player injury economy: starting bandages, first
 Treat/Repair free, two new facilities, button visibility

- 2 free Field Bandages in a new guild's starting inventory (root
  cause confirmed: 50 starting gold can't afford either existing
  cure -- Treat 70-90g, buying a bandage 60g).
- New Hero.usedFreeTreat/usedFreeRepair: each hero's first Treat and
  first Repair ever are free, no gold cost.
- Two new guild facilities, Physician's Charity and Smith's Charity
  (5 levels each, 1 free Treat/Repair per day per level, guild-wide).
  New GuildDef.freeHealsPerLevel/freeRepairsPerLevel structural
  fields; ModifierManager.freeHealsPerDay/freeRepairsPerDay reads
  them.
- GameEngine.consumeFreeHeal/consumeFreeRepair: guild's renewable
  daily allowance spends first, hero's one-time freebie is the
  fallback -- verified both apply in that order before gold is ever
  touched. Wired into treatInjury, repair, and repairAll (batch-safe,
  applies per item/hero). Auto-repair's background tick deliberately
  left untouched -- freebies stay a deliberate, noticed action.
- New GuidanceManager topic (first_injury_or_wear): one combined
  notification for both systems, explicitly states first Treat/Repair
  are free and the rest cost gold, points at Heroes tab.
- Treat/Bandage/Repair/Repair-everything buttons were bare unstyled
  <button> elements with no class at all -- root cause of them being
  effectively invisible. All four now use .btn-primary, show 'Free'
  in the label when a freebie is available, and the collapsed hero
  card's injury summary now hints '(expand to Treat)'.
- guild-idler-status.md updated with full writeup.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and vite build both clean. Runtime-verified:
starting bandage count; first-treat-free then gold-required-and-failing
second treat; guild-daily-then-personal priority order with both
available; daily allowance resetting on a simulated day boundary;
single-item and batch repair both freebie-aware across multiple
items/heroes; new facilities purchasable via the existing generic
GuildManager.upgradeFacility; the guidance topic firing on a simulated
injury; and a simulated pre-patch save (every new field deleted)
migrating and playing through treatInjury with zero crashes.
